+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+On the adversarial synthetic store (50,000 records drawn from the benchmark's
+30-word frequent vocabulary, with 2,000 rare identifier variants), the measured
+full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` p95 was **51.240912 ms** before the term-selection
+fix (300 runs).
+
+The fix was to discard a candidate prompt term before the top-8 IDF selection
+when it occurs in more than one third of a store of at least 50 records. Such a
+term carries little signal on this workload and makes FTS5 traverse a long
+posting list. The selector still drops terms absent from the store, scores the
+remaining terms by IDF, and sends at most eight terms to BM25.
+
+With that fix, the measured full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` p95 was
+**6.046097 ms** on the same 50,000-record, 300-run benchmark.
